Build **Facet**, a gem-matching puzzle that runs entirely in the browser, and
produce the art, the effects, and the sound it plays yourself during this build.

Your project root is `{{workspace}}`. Build the game there.

## What to read first

The full specification is in the `specs/` directory at `{{workspace}}`, already
present in your project. Produce an implementation that matches the
specification exactly. `specs/overview.md` is the entry point: it says how the
rest of the specification is organized, what you implement, which files stay as
they are, the code quality the build is held to, and the commands that run over
the finished repository. `specs/assets.md` is the production contract for the
art, the effects, and the sound the game plays: it names the tools on your
`PATH`, what each one produces, and how the produced files are wired in. The
project's own `README.md` describes the workspace as it was seeded.

